{"entries":[{"id":"scofield-es-deu-1-2","title":"Deuteronomio 1:2","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Introducción al libro - Deuteronomio Lea el primer capítulo de Deuteronomio DEUTERONOMIO consiste en los consejos de despedida que Moisés dio a Israel en vista de la inminente entrada en su posesión pactada. Contiene un resumen de los vagabundeos de Israel en el desierto, que es importante para desarrollar el juicio moral de Dios sobre esos eventos; repite el Decálogo a una generación que había crecido en el desierto; da la instrucción necesaria sobre la conducta de Israel en la tierra y contiene el Pacto Palestino (Deuteronomio 30:1-9). El libro respira la severidad de la Ley. Palabras clave: &quot;Tú deberás&quot;; versículos clave, Deuteronomio 11:26-28. Es importante señalar que, si bien la tierra prometida fue dada incondicionalmente a Abraham y a su descendencia en el Pacto Abrahámico (Génesis 13:15; 15:7), fue bajo el Pacto Palestino condicional (Deuteronomio 28:1-30:9) que Israel entró en la tierra bajo Josué. Violando por completo las condiciones de ese pacto, la nación primero fue perturbada (1 Reyes 12) y luego expulsada de la tierra (2 Reyes 17:1-18; 24:1-25:11). Pero el mismo pacto promete incondicionalmente una restauración nacional de Israel que aún no se ha cumplido (véase Scofield &quot;De 15:18&quot;). DEUTERONOMIO está dividido en siete divisiones: Resumen de la historia de Israel en el desierto, 1:1-3:29 Una reformulación de la Ley, con advertencias y exhortaciones, 4:1 -11:32, Instrucciones, advertencias y predicciones, 12:1-27:26, Las grandes profecías finales que resumen la historia de Israel hasta la segunda venida de Cristo y que contienen el Pacto palestino, 28:1-30:20, Últimos consejos a los sacerdotes, levitas y a Josué, 31, El cántico de Moisés y sus bendiciones de despedida, 32,33, La muerte de Moisés, 34. El tiempo que abarca esta retrospectiva es de aproximadamente cuarenta años. once días Prolongado por un acto de incredulidad a cuarenta años. (véase Scofield &quot;Números 14:23&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-1-2","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-1-3","title":"Deuteronomio 1:3","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>undécimo, es decir, febrero.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-1-3","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-2-9","title":"Deuteronomio 2:9","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>dada Ar Una región al este del Mar Muerto.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-2-9","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-3-17","title":"Deuteronomio 3:17","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>Ashdoth-pisgah, es decir, los manantiales de Pisgah, o la colina.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-3-17","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-4-10","title":"Deuteronomio 4:10","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-4-10","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-4-15","title":"Deuteronomio 4:15","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>no vio ninguna manera Cf. (véase Scofield &quot;Juan 1:18&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-4-15","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-5-29","title":"Deuteronomio 5:29","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-5-29","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-6-13","title":"Deuteronomio 6:13","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-6-13","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-7-8","title":"Deuteronomio 7:8","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>redimido (véase Scofield &quot;Éxodo 14:30&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-7-8","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-8-6","title":"Deuteronomio 8:6","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-8-6","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-9-10","title":"Deuteronomio 9:10","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Y el Señor (véase Scofield &quot;Éxodo 20:4&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-9-10","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-9-26","title":"Deuteronomio 9:26","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>redimido (véase Scofield &quot;Éxodo 14:30&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-9-26","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-10-3","title":"Deuteronomio 10:3","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Shittim, es decir, acacia.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-10-3","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-10-12","title":"Deuteronomio 10:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-10-12","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-10-20","title":"Deuteronomio 10:20","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-10-20","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-13-4","title":"Deuteronomio 13:4","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":13,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":13,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-13-4","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-13-5","title":"Deuteronomio 13:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":13,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":13,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>redimido (véase Scofield &quot;Éxodo 14:30&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-13-5","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-14-7","title":"Deuteronomio 14:7","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>liebre (véase Scofield &quot;Levítico 11:6&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-14-7","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-14-23","title":"Deuteronomio 14:23","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-14-23","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-15-15","title":"Deuteronomio 15:15","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>redimido Ver nota, (véase Scofield &quot;Éxodo 14:30&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-15-15","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-16-1","title":"Deuteronomio 16:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>guardar la pascua Cf. el orden de las fiestas en Lev. 23. Aquí se da especial énfasis a la Pascua y los Tabernáculos como marcando el comienzo y la consumación de los caminos de Dios con Israel; el primero habla de la redención, el fundamento de todo; el segundo, o Israel reunido y bendecido en el reino. En el medio, en Deuteronomio 16:9-12 viene la Fiesta de las Semanas: el gozo de un pueblo redimido, que anticipa una bendición mayor aún por venir. Es, moralmente, Romanos 5:1,2. Abib Primer mes, es decir, abril.</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-16-1","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-16-21","title":"Deuteronomio 16:21","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>bosque sagrado Los bosques sagrados (heb. Asherim) mencionados tan a menudo en el A.T. estaban dedicados al culto de Astoret, la diosa babilónica Ishtar, la Afrodita de los griegos, la Venus romana. Cf. (véase Scofield &quot;Jueces 2:13&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-16-21","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-17-19","title":"Deuteronomio 17:19","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-17-19","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-19-6","title":"Deuteronomio 19:6","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>vengador heb. &quot;goel&quot;, redimir. (Tipo pariente). (véase Scofield &quot;Isaías 59:20&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-19-6","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-21-8","title":"Deuteronomio 21:8","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Israel (véase Scofield &quot;Éxodo 14:30&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-21-8","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-24-18","title":"Deuteronomio 24:18","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>redimido (véase Scofield &quot;Éxodo 14:30&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-24-18","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-28-1","title":"Deuteronomio 28:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>si escuchas los Capítulos 28.-29. son, propiamente, una parte integral del pacto palestino, Deuteronomio 30:1-9. (véase Scofield &quot;Deuteronomio 30:3&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-28-1","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-28-52","title":"Deuteronomio 28:52","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":52,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":52},"content":"<p>más confiable (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 2:12&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-28-52","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-28-58","title":"Deuteronomio 28:58","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":58,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":58},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-28-58","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-30-3","title":"Deuteronomio 30:3","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Convierte tu cautiverio El Pacto Palestino da las condiciones bajo las cuales Israel entró en la tierra prometida. Es importante ver que la nación nunca ha tomado todavía la tierra bajo el Pacto Abrahámico incondicional, ni ha poseído toda la tierra (cf. Génesis 15:18; Números 34:1-12. El Pacto Palestino está dividido en siete partes. (1) Dispersión por desobediencia, Deuteronomio 30:1; 28:63-68 (véase Scofield &quot;Génesis 15:18&quot;) (2) El futuro arrepentimiento de Israel mientras estaba en dispersión, Deuteronomio 30:2. (3) El regreso del Señor, Deuteronomio 30:3; Amós 9:9-14; Jeremías 23:3-8; 37:21-25 (5) Conversión nacional, Deuteronomio 30:6; Romanos 11:26,27; Oseas 2:14-16 (6) Prosperidad nacional, Deuteronomio 30:9; 9:11-14 Para otro punto de vista: Ver Tema 301242 Ver, para los otros siete pactos: EDENIC (véase Scofield &quot;Génesis 1:28&quot;) ADAMIC véase Scofield &quot;Génesis 3:15&quot; ABRAHAMIC véase Scofield &quot;Génesis 15:18&quot; NOAHIC véase Scofield &quot;Génesis 9:1&quot; MOSAIC véase Scofield &quot;Éxodo 19:25&quot; DAVIDIC véase Scofield &quot;2 Samuel 7:16&quot; NUEVO véase Scofield &quot;Hebreos 8:8&quot;</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-30-3","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-31-12","title":"Deuteronomio 31:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>miedo (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 19:9&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-31-12","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-32-36","title":"Deuteronomio 32:36","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>arrepentirse (véase Scofield &quot;Zacarías 8:14&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-32-36","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-32-37","title":"Deuteronomio 32:37","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":32,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":32,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>confiable (véase Scofield &quot;Salmo 2:12&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-32-37","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}},{"id":"scofield-es-deu-33-8","title":"Deuteronomio 33:8","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":33,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":33,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Tumim (véase Scofield &quot;Éxodo 28:30&quot;).</p>","translation":{"sourceId":"scofield-deu-33-8","status":"official","sourceLanguage":"en","targetLanguage":"es"}}]}
